# bytes are never committed.  most of these licences prohibit redistribution, and
# the catalogue we draw from is 2.55 PB.  the repository commits cards, recipes and
# manifests -- what a source is, how it was derived, and what the result hashed to.
sources/*/raw/**
!sources/*/raw/.location.yaml
!sources/*/raw/checksums.txt
sources/*/evidence/**
# a directory excluded by `**` cannot have a file inside it re-included, so the
# recipe directories have to be un-excluded before the manifest can be.  without
# these two lines the negation below silently does nothing and every manifest is
# dropped -- which is the opposite of what the paragraph above says this file is for.
!sources/*/evidence/*/
!sources/*/evidence/*/manifest.yaml
# and `measured.json` beside it: a few tens of kB of numbers a recipe produced,
# which is the same kind of thing as a manifest and not the same kind of thing as
# the arrays.  ibm/topologies/tract_prior.py reads one at import, so leaving it
# out would mean a fresh checkout silently ran on compiled-in constants.
!sources/*/evidence/*/measured.json
index/**/*.jsonl
!index/neuro2/candidates.jsonl
index/**/*.json.gz
